Plugging in AC triggers ml-service because it has smart charging support used
by powerd. Since we don't really need this job in the factory, we disable it
here.

ml-service holds stateful partition after `stop ml-service` so it breaks
`clobber-state factory` in the CrOS device factory finalization. Check
b/241077407.
